From c310eabea51ea2280bc829594bb9da33b77b845e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:03:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a CI wait on a run that can never start is
 refused at park and woken while parked

A hub card parked (awaiting kind=ci) on GitHub Actions run 42993449998 whose jobs asked for
self-hosted,ci-fast runners that no longer took jobs; _check_run only checked the ref looked like a
run id, so the card slept until David asked (self-heal defect agent-c2b8fc1abf).

kanban_ci_progress.ci_run_progress reads a run's jobs (gh api) and reports not_starting when a job
has been queued > 15 min with no runner. A kind=ci park on such a run is refused
(ci_run_unstartable, labels named) in confirm_remote, before the write txn. The wake-check tick
re-reads every CI-waiting card's run at most every 5 min (off the dispatcher thread) and wakes a
not-starting one with a comment and the shared blocker runners-offline.<labels> asserted on it.
GitHub errors fail open (logged).
